course: dictionary
lesson: 1521
title: Reading the clues in a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can look like it means one thing, but the sentence around it tells you what it really means. «Despite their name, no centipede has exactly one hundred legs.» The name sounds as if it means a hundred legs, but the sentence says that is not true. Despite means even though, so the clue shows the name is misleading.
explain: Look for words that show a difference. «Millipedes have two pairs of legs on most body sections and centipedes have one pair, which is how you tell them apart.» The words which is how you tell them apart are a big clue: the number of leg pairs is the difference between the two creatures.
explain: Always check your meaning. Put your idea into the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: A centipede is a long, thin creature with a flat body divided into many parts.
fact: Each part of a centipede's body has one pair of legs.
fact: Centipedes are fast hunters that live in dark, damp places and eat insects.
fact: Centipedes are not insects, because insects have six legs.
fact: «Millipedes» have two pairs of legs on most body sections, are slow, and eat dead plants.
exercise: A centipede is a long, thin creature with a flat body in many parts. How many pairs of legs does each body part have? | *One pair | Six pairs | No legs at all | Two pairs
exercise: «Despite their name, no centipede has exactly one hundred legs.» What does despite mean here? | Before | Instead of | Because of | *Even though
exercise: Is a centipede an insect? | *No, insects have six legs and centipedes do not | Yes, because it lives in damp places | Yes, because it hunts insects | Yes, it is a small insect
test: «Millipedes have two pairs of legs on most body sections.» Which creature has one pair of legs on each body section? | Woodlouse | *Centipede | Millipede | Insect
test: Ella says centipedes are slow and eat dead plants, like millipedes. What is wrong with what she says? | Centipedes have exactly one hundred legs | Centipedes have two pairs of legs | *Centipedes are fast hunters that eat insects | Centipedes live in deserts
exam: A centipede is fast and hunts insects in dark, damp places. What does hunts most likely mean? | Builds a nest from leaves | Sleeps all day under a stone | Sings loudly at night | *Chases and catches animals for food
